.DS_Store
*.log
.idea/
.wrangler/
__pycache__/
.worktrees/
.superpowers/
# Codex CLI runtime state: .codex/ doubles as this repo's project-level
# CODEX_HOME, so any codex-family binary run from the repo root writes its own
# per-install state here (state/logs/memories/queue/goals SQLite DBs + WAL/SHM
# sidecars, installation_id, version.json, skills/.system/, tmp/ and .tmp/, and
# potentially auth.json). Only three things are tracked, so this is default-deny
# with those three re-included, rather than a list of the filenames Codex happens
# to write today — a new runtime file must not be able to appear as untracked,
# and auth.json must never become committable. A file added under .codex/ on
# purpose later needs its own negation line here. Use `.codex/*` rather than
# `.codex/` so git still traverses into the directory; a bare `.codex/` would
# prevent the re-includes. Anchored to root (worktree copies are already covered
# by .worktrees/).
.codex/*
!.codex/agents/
!.codex/config.toml
!.codex/model-profiles.lock.toml
# Ignore everything in .claude/ EXCEPT the project-scoped skills + agents trees
# (which are tracked so skill/agent definitions survive fresh clones / propagate
# to CI). Use `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/` so git still traverses
# into the directory; a bare `.claude/` would prevent the re-include.
# __pycache__ and .DS_Store stay ignored via the top-of-file rules.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/agents/
# Re-include fixture scaffolding under setup test fixtures (gitignore '.claude/' matches anywhere)
!tests/fixtures/setup/*/input/.claude/
!tests/fixtures/setup/*/input/.claude/**

# Fixture runtime artifacts — the lock file, config, logs, and SQLite WAL/SHM
# sidecars regenerate on every harness run and are never committed. (The
# consumed-from-tree dashboard/share/migrations/doctor/projects fixtures DO
# commit their stats.db/cache.db; the scratch-rebuild suites do not — see the
# block below and #97.)
cache.db*.lock
cache.db-wal
cache.db-shm
stats.db-wal
stats.db-shm
# The migrations fixtures name their databases `*.sqlite`, so the `.db` entries
# above never matched their sidecars (#566).
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
tests/fixtures/*/*/.local/share/ccusage-subscription/config.json
tests/fixtures/*/*/.local/share/ccusage-subscription/logs/
tests/fixtures/*/*/.local/share/cctally/config.json
tests/fixtures/*/*/.local/share/cctally/logs/

# Scratch-rebuild harness suites: their {stats,cache}.db are NEVER read — the
# harness rebuilds fresh into a `--out <scratch>` dir on every run (see #97), so
# committed copies drift silently to stale schemas with no test catching it.
# Don't track them; `bin/build-<cmd>-fixtures.py` regenerates on demand. The
# consumed-from-tree fixtures (dashboard, share, migrations + per-migration
# goldens, doctor, projects) are deliberately absent here — their committed
# .db ARE the test input and stay tracked.
tests/fixtures/alerts/*/.local/share/cctally/*.db
tests/fixtures/blocks/*/.local/share/cctally/*.db
tests/fixtures/cache-report/*/.local/share/cctally/*.db
tests/fixtures/daily/*/.local/share/cctally/*.db
tests/fixtures/monthly/*/.local/share/cctally/*.db
tests/fixtures/report/*/.local/share/cctally/*.db
tests/fixtures/codex-daily/*/.local/share/cctally/*.db
tests/fixtures/codex-monthly/*/.local/share/cctally/*.db
tests/fixtures/codex-session/*/.local/share/cctally/*.db
tests/fixtures/codex-weekly/*/.local/share/cctally/*.db
tests/fixtures/diff/*/.local/share/cctally/*.db
tests/fixtures/forecast/*/.local/share/cctally/*.db
tests/fixtures/project/*/.local/share/cctally/*.db
tests/fixtures/session/*/.local/share/cctally/*.db
tests/fixtures/weekly/*/.local/share/cctally/*.db

# === npm root install pollution ===
# `package.json` at the repo root is the npm-publish sentinel; npm's natural
# workflow puts `node_modules/` and `package-lock.json` next to it on any
# `npm install <pkg>` from root. Anchor to root so dashboard/web's legitimate
# Vite/React deps (handled by dashboard/web/.gitignore) stay untouched.
/node_modules
/package-lock.json

# === Browser-MCP artifacts ===
# Playwright MCP writes a page snapshot + console log to .playwright-mcp/ on
# every browser interaction. This one stays ignored because the MCP server
# writes it unconditionally rather than because a QA run chose to keep it;
# un-ignoring it would make every browser-driven run dirty by construction.
.playwright-mcp/
#
# Root-level QA evidence is deliberately NOT ignored. Rules naming
# /share-v2-smoke*.png, baseline/ and /cctally-qa-*/ used to sit here, from the
# era when a QA pass dumped screenshots at the repo root and left them. The
# UI-QA contract now requires every screenshot to be deleted at cleanup
# (.agent-workflows/contracts/ui-qa.md), and the guard's before/after source
# hash enumerates `git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard`
# (.agent-workflows/lib/ui_qa_guard.py:44), which skips ignored files. An
# ignore rule over that evidence would hide the exact cleanup failure the gate
# exists to catch: leftovers would not move the hash, so a run that abandoned
# them would still certify. Left visible, a missed cleanup both dirties
# `git status` and fails the gate. Retained reports belong in
# .agent-workflows/reports/ui-qa/, which is tracked and committed with the work
# it certifies; nothing else a QA run produces belongs in the tree at all.
.agentmem/local/

# Screenshot-pipeline output manifest (README_SCREENSHOTS_OUT_DIR contract artifact,
# consumed by cctally-release readme-refresh; regenerated every run, never published)
docs/img/manifest.json

# Machine-owned roots the runner provisions and the transport never converges
# (#529 S3). Listing them here aligns git's view with their status, so a
# maintainer with a local .venv does not have it selected into the staged tree
# and refused as a path inside a runner-owned root.
/.venv/
/.cctally-remote-state/
